# 2) Layer 4 vs Layer 7

# Layer 4 (Transport Layer)

Works with:
- TCP
- UDP
- Ports

Can see:
- Source IP
- Destination IP
- Port number

Cannot see:
- URL
- Headers
- Payload

Example:
443 → Backend VM

Routing based on:
- IP
- Port

Security Concerns:
- Port scanning
- DDoS attacks
- SYN flood
- Unauthorized access

Protection:
- NSG
- Firewall
- Rate limiting

---

# Layer 7 (Application Layer)

Works with:
- HTTP
- HTTPS

Can inspect:
- URL
- Headers
- Cookies
- Request body

Example:
/api → Backend1
/admin → Backend2

Security Concerns:
- SQL Injection
- XSS
- CSRF
- Session hijacking
- API abuse

Protection:
- WAF
- Authentication
- API Gateway
- Input validation

Traffic Flow:

Internet
   |
WAF/Application Gateway
   |
Web Server
   |
App Server
   |
Database

